Actually precisely: after `exit $EXIT_CODE`, the `result`, `directive`, `ended_because`, `reported`, `chain_continues`, `changed` outputs are NOT written. So downstream conditions see empty for those. saveSessionStep still runs (always(), outcome != skipped) — the session file may or may not exist (atoma saves the session itself at its own intervals? The out-session is written by atoma run — if atoma crashed, the session file is whatever atoma last wrote... the doc says "The session was saved" — saveAgentSession reads `${RUN_DIR}/session.json`... if atoma died before writing anything, the session file might be the RESTORED one (from restoreSessionStep writing it into RUN_DIR) — in which case saving it is a no-op-ish (saves the restored session, losing nothing new). OK, the "session was saved" claim: saveSessionStep runs and saves what exists. Fine.

